# supercronic crontab for the merge-queue arming sweep (GOL-3159).
#
# Every 5 minutes. That number is measured, not guessed (see the cadence table in
# scripts/ci/merge-queue-arm-sweep.sh): across the last 39 agent PRs that were
# enqueued by `github-actions[bot]`, the open->enqueue window had a median of 23
# min but a MINIMUM of 1.6 min, and 5 min is the knee of the catch-rate curve --
# ~96% of wedges caught, versus 88% at 10 min and 49% hourly. Going finer than
# 5 min buys the last 4% for 5x the API calls; going coarser loses real wedges.
#
# A fire costs 2 GitHub API calls per repo (one token mint, one GraphQL read)
# plus one carve-out fetch per repo that has unapproved PRs -- roughly 100
# requests/hour against a 5000/hour installation-token budget.
#
# Over-running is cheap and safe: the sweep is idempotent. A second pass reads
# "already armed by agenticos-developer" and no-ops.
*/5 * * * * /app/scripts/ci/merge-queue-arm-sweep.sh --apply
